Hi Christian,

The fact that there are some rows with "0,0,0" makes me suspect that the idle sleep mode by ActiGraph was activated. However, I think ActiLife changed the way in which they imputed these periods, they used to impute them with "0,0,0", but then they changed it to the last observation carried forward. Are you using an old version of ActiLife?

Also, I have never seen that the idle sleep mode gets activated in the very beginning of the file and, as such, I have never encountered this issue. We were working on handling the idle sleep mode some time ago and we made GGIR account for it in most scenarios, but this could be an exception. Just for curiosity, did you split this file somehow? By definition, the idle sleep mode gets activated when the device detects no movement for 10 consecutive seconds (https://actigraphcorp.my.site.com/support/s/article/Idle-Sleep-Mode-Explained), so the very first rows of the file should never be "0,0,0".

Best,
Jairo

