Dear Vincent

Yes, it is an older GT3x that sadly is not supported. The serial number of the Actigraphs start with CPW.

I have here three times the same file in different variants for you that have 0,0,0\n at the beginning. Due to size limitations I've uploaded them to Google Drive.

GT3x direct download from centrepoint  --> this cannot be read in directly to GGIR since this GT3X version is not supported afaik
https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GN80KyqpgP8sKvaIRc66MzVif-tFuJzN/view?usp=share_link

csv converted from GT3X with ActiLife 6.13.4  --> this cannot be read in directly to GGIR due to the 0,0,0\t at the beginning. After removal it can be read. Other files without the 0,0,0 can be read in directly without problems.
https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qXxEqpxr3oBXOfcT9yxpS-ly3ABDsKh7/view?usp=share_link

CSV direct download from centrepoint (huge, about 1 GB, because it includes timestamps)  --> this cannot be read in directly to GGIR (more information concering this issue are here: https://groups.google.com/g/RpackageGGIR/c/AOOnKdA3FkM)
https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FC1UfCPMc0YtMK0TU1Pa4H690-lcbgD2/view?usp=share_link

Best regards!
Christian

